  Easy names at home


  The internet
  self-host opens no port on your router. Do not forward port 80 to this
  computer; these pages are meant for your home network.

  Changing it later
  Everything here can be changed later in Settings, under Access.

  Technical details
  One managed Caddy in the Compose Project owns port 80 and routes HTTP
  requests by Host to each App. Names are <app>.<lan-ip-with-dashes>.sslip.io
  on every OS. sslip.io sees the LAN address in DNS queries. DNS-rebind
  protection can block names; the IP:port Address stays. Port conflicts and
  rootless Docker are refused without changes. HTTP is not encrypted; Apps
  that require HTTPS still require it. A DHCP reservation keeps bookmarks
  stable.

